Why rag is required when LLM is already powerful
	LLMS doesn’t know your private/company data 
	LLM knowledge can be outdated, it can hallucinate
	Don’t need to retrain LLM every time when data changes
	Rag provides sources/ citations

Is rag still relevant in the era of long context LLMS
	Yes, rag is still important even with large-context LLMs
	Large context models have limitation:
		Lost-in-the-middle
		Higher API costs
		Increased latency 
	As context becomes large it's tough for the LLM to find the most relevant information effects the quality of responses, processing large amounts of text for every request increases the tokens so cost and latency were effected
	
Challenges of RAG Systems?
	Retrieval problems?                                Generation problems?
		Wrong chunks                                      hallucination
		Poor chunking                                      poor reasoning                       
		Bad embedding                                    context overload
		Query ambiguity                                  unsupported answer
		Stale documents 
		
Effective strategies to reduce latency in RAG systems?
	Reduces the no. of retrieved documents
	Use a fast vector database
	Reduce or limit unnecessary re ranking
	Parallelize independent operations
	Reduce LLM calls
	User faster and smaller models
	Reduce context size
	Cache the embedding's and generally asked questions and responses
	
Explain R,A,G in RAG?
	R- retrieval   process of searching and fetching the most relevant information from the external knowledge sources for the given user query
	A-Augmented  includes retrieved context, instructions, query in the prompt 
	G-Generation generator LLM process the prompt to generate a response  that is accurate and relevant
